              "type": "text",
              "text": "I need to verify that the anonymous GitHub repo was properly synced with the latest paper files. A previous agent claimed only 4 files changed, but the Director says there were extensive modifications since 5/23 (data fixes, table updates, figure fixes, citation audit fixes on 5/24 and 5/26).\n\nThe repo is at: https://[REDACTED]@github.com/anonymous-nlp-2026-2/irt_personfit_contam.git\n\nThe latest paper source is at: /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/paper/\n\nPlease do the following:\n\n1. Clone the repo fresh to /tmp/anon_verify (remove if exists first)\n2. Compare key files that should have changed:\n   - Compare `paper/sections/results.tex` in repo vs source (`paper/sections/results.tex` in source dir) - use `diff` command\n   - Compare `paper/sections/experiments.tex` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/sections/introduction.tex` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/references.bib` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/main.tex` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/main.bbl` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/sections/discussion.tex` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/sections/appendix.tex` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `paper/sections/abstract.tex` in repo vs source\n   - Compare `src/person_fit.py` in repo vs source (`paper/src/person_fit.py`)\n   - Compare `qwen/*.py` in repo vs source (`paper/qwen/*.py`)\n   - Compare `requirements.txt` in repo vs source (`paper/requirements.txt`)\n\n3. For each comparison, just show whether they differ (not the full diff). Use something like:\n   ```\n   diff /tmp/anon_verify/paper/sections/results.tex /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/paper/sections/results.tex > /dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"SAME\" || echo \"DIFFERS\"\n   ```\n\n4. Also check if there are files in the source that don't exist in the repo:\n   - List all .py files in source paper/qwen/, paper/llama/, paper/mistral/, paper/scripts/\n   - Compare with repo qwen/, llama/, mistral/, scripts/\n\n5. Check the README for:\n   - Does it still contain the old title \"IRT Person-Fit Statistics for LLM Benchmark Contamination Detection\"?\n   - Does it contain any \"anonymous.4open.science\" URLs?\n\n6. Report which files DIFFER and which are SAME. If many files differ, that means the sync was incomplete and we need to redo it.\n\nNOTE: Redirect all stdout/stderr to files under /tmp/ and read them back if bash has issues with direct output."
            }
